        "description": "During the 2026 \"Bond with Kuliang\" China-US Youth Baseball Exhibition Games and Sports Festival in Fuzhou, young American baseball players stepped beyond the field to experience touhu (pitch-pot), a traditional Chinese game with a history of more than 2,000 years.\nOriginating from ancient archery rituals, touhu challenges players to toss arrow-like sticks into a narrow-necked pot, blending precision, etiquette and friendly competition.\nThe cultural experience offered the young visitors a fun way to connect with Chinese traditions while building friendships through sports.",
